   The dynamics of the double‑pendulum are highly nonlinear; a fixed velocity threshold works only for a narrow part of the swing. When the arm is moving fast (`|v2|≈2‑4`) the controller still treats it as “small’’ and may output `action=1` (no torque), letting the system lose momentum.

