| **`h > 0.88` + `v_tip > 0`** | Guarantees we only stop when the tip is already moving downward, eliminating the “stop‑too‑early’’ problem that produced many ‑80‑reward runs. |
| **`v_tip = v1+v2`** | Uses the *combined* momentum of both joints; when the first link is still swinging upward it contributes positively, giving the controller more information than `v2` alone. |
| **Higher `v2` thresholds (0.30 / 0.35)** | Prevents the controller from “fighting’’ the momentum when the second joint is already fast – we only change torque direction when the sign of `v2·s2` says we are braking. |
| **Small dead‑zone on `s2` (±0.07)** | Avoids chattering when the second link is almost aligned; the policy will stay at `action=1` and let the inertia carry the tip over the barrier. |
| **Separate “priming’’ and “balancing’’ phases** | Keeps the proven energy‑pumping behaviour for the first half‑swing while adding a more nuanced decision in the second half. |

