| **Coupling with joint‑1** | Ignored `v1`. | Added `k_f * v1` – when the first link is already swinging upward, its angular velocity can be used to “ride the wave” and push the second link in the same direction. | Less wasted torque, smoother swing‑up. |
| **Damping** | No explicit damping; sometimes overshoot caused the tip to fall back. | `-k_d * v2` reduces torque when `v2` is large, preventing the second link from whipping past the upright position. | More stable approach to the target height. |
| **Cosine bias** | No knowledge of the relative orientation of the second link (`c2`). | `k_c * c2` adds a small bias that automatically reduces torque when the second link already points upwards (`c2 < 0`). | Avoids “pushing against” the already‑upright second link. |
| **Fine‑balance dead‑zone** | Fixed thresholds (`|v2| > 0.35`, `|s2| > 0.15`). | Scales torque down when `|s2|` is tiny and adds a proportional bias `0.2 * (-s2)`. | Improves holding the tip near the top, reduces oscillations that otherwise drive the tip back down. |
