| **Fast downward motion after a high swing** (`c1≈‑0.2, s2≈‑0.8, v2≈‑0.7, h≈0.88`) | torque = `‑0.6·(‑0.8)‑0.4·(‑0.7)‑0.2·(‑0.12) ≈ +0.92` → `action=2` | Right torque pushes the joint forward, turning the downward swing into a new upward swing. |

All of these behaviours line up with the intuition of a swing‑up / balance controller.

