The **sign‑product swing‑up rule** is the most effective part we have discovered, but the controller still lacks a **balancing** component for the final stage (when the tip is close to the target height).  Adding a small proportional‑derivative (PD) term on `v2` (and optionally on `v1`) once the height error is small will keep the tip from falling back, while keeping the simple sign‑product rule for the high‑energy swing‑up part.

